<div class="task-intro"><div><span class="eyebrow">Self-service guide</span><p>Start with a suitable template and build the talk around your audience.</p></div><a href="$link.page('CRH', 'Slide Decks & Presentations')" class="button">Find presentation resources</a></div><section class="reading-section"><h2>Build the story</h2><ul><li>Give each slide a clear purpose and use readable, concise headings.</li><li>Use the supplied layouts and keep spacing, alignment and typography consistent.</li><li>Use imagery and charts to explain the message; retain their sources and credits.</li></ul></section><section class="reading-section"><h2>Check before presenting</h2><ul><li>Try the deck on the intended display and check that text and charts are readable from the audience’s position.</li><li>Check contrast, alternative text and reading order. Caption any video.</li><li>Check facts, dates and any adapted claims with the appropriate content owner.</li></ul></section><aside class="next-step"><div><h2>Need more than formatting?</h2><p>Bring the draft and audience brief.</p></div><a href="$link.page('CRH', 'Submitting a Request')" class="text-link">Ask for a review</a></aside><nav class="section-next" aria-label="More in Presentations"><div class="section-next-head"><h2>More in Presentations</h2><a class="related-all" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Slide Decks & Presentations')">Prepare a presentation →</a></div><div class="related-grid"><a class="related-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Standard SKAO Template')"><span class="related-next">Next</span><strong>Standard SKAO template</strong><span>A starting layout for a presentation using your own content.</span></a><a class="related-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Widescreen Template')"><strong>Widescreen template</strong><span>A 16:9 starting layout for suitable screens and webinars.</span></a><a class="related-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'About SKAO Master Deck')"><strong>About SKAO master deck</strong><span>An overview for institutional introductions and general briefings.</span></a></div></nav>
