<div class="task-intro"><div><span class="eyebrow">New work or a review</span><p>Choose how you want to start. Either way, the team replies to agree the scope and timing with you.</p></div></div><div class="route-choice"><a class="route-card primary" href="https://jira.skatelescope.org/servicedesk/customer/portal/364"><span class="eyebrow">I have a brief</span><strong>Submit it in the helpdesk</strong><span>Attach your files or source links. The team replies to agree scope and timing.</span><em>Open creative helpdesk ↗</em></a><a class="route-card" href="#brief-builder" data-open-details><span class="eyebrow">I need help</span><strong>Write my brief here</strong><span>Answer six short questions, then copy the result into the helpdesk.</span><em>Start the brief helper ↓</em></a></div><div class="process-strip"><span><b>1</b> Describe the need</span><span><b>2</b> Submit in Jira</span><span><b>3</b> Agree scope and timing</span></div><details class="brief-builder" id="brief-builder"><summary>Need help writing the brief?</summary><div class="builder-content"><p>Use this optional helper, then copy the result into Jira. It does not submit a request.</p><p class="form-note">Fields marked * are required. Your draft is not saved and is lost if you leave or reload.</p><form id="briefForm" hidden><div class="form-grid"><label class="field">Project *<input name="Project" required maxlength="3000" type="text"><small>What is the work called?</small></label><label class="field">Use date *<input name="Use date" required maxlength="3000" type="text"><small>When will it be used, and why then?</small></label><label class="field">Purpose and audience *<textarea name="Purpose and audience" required maxlength="3000"></textarea><small>What should this help people understand or do?</small></label><label class="field">Outputs and scope *<textarea name="Outputs and scope" required maxlength="3000"></textarea><small>What do you need? Include format, quantity and what is out of scope.</small></label><label class="field">Content and review owners<textarea name="Content and review owners"  maxlength="3000"></textarea><small>Who supplies the content and who approves the result?</small></label><label class="field">Inputs and constraints<textarea name="Inputs and constraints"  maxlength="3000"></textarea><small>Source links, budget, rights, missing information and dependencies.</small></label></div><button class="button" type="submit">Prepare my request</button></form><section id="draftPanel" hidden><h2 id="draftHeading" tabindex="-1">Your request draft</h2><p>Review the wording, copy it, then submit it in the helpdesk. A request is not booked until scope and timing are confirmed.</p><pre class="output" id="briefOutput"></pre><div class="actions"><button id="copyBrief" class="button" type="button">Copy request text</button><a href="https://jira.skatelescope.org/servicedesk/customer/portal/364" class="button secondary">Open helpdesk to submit</a></div><p id="copyStatus" class="status" role="status"></p></section></div></details><noscript><p>Use the creative helpdesk directly. The optional brief helper needs JavaScript.</p></noscript><details class="guidance-detail"><summary>What makes a useful brief?</summary><div><section class="reading-section"><h2>Include these essentials</h2><ul><li>Purpose, audience and the real use date.</li><li>Outputs, formats and what is outside the scope.</li><li>Draft content, source material and any missing inputs.</li><li>Content owner, final reviewer, budget and supplier constraints.</li></ul></section></div></details><aside class="next-step"><div><h2>A request is the start of a conversation</h2><p>The team confirms capacity, scope and delivery timing after review.</p></div><a href="$link.page('CRH', 'Turnaround Times')" class="text-link">How timing is agreed</a></aside><p class="quiet-note">Planning an event? <a href="$link.page('CRH', 'Events Support')" class="">Brief the creative materials</a>. Event logistics stay with the events team.</p><nav class="section-next" aria-label="More in Get help"><div class="section-next-head"><h2>More in Get help</h2><a class="related-all" href="$link.page('CRH', 'How To Work With Us')">Work with Creative Production →</a></div><div class="related-grid"><a class="related-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'What We Can Help With')"><span class="related-next">Next</span><strong>What we can help with</strong><span>Creative Production helps shape and produce agreed creative materials. The brief determines the work and the capacity required.</span></a><a class="related-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Turnaround Times')"><strong>Agree scope and timing</strong><span>Give the actual use date and explain what depends on it. Delivery timing is agreed after the brief and capacity are reviewed.</span></a><a class="related-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Requesting New Video Content')"><strong>Brief video or animation</strong><span>Check existing footage first, then explain what a new piece needs to achieve.</span></a></div></nav>
