<div class="task-intro"><div><span class="eyebrow">Make the work usable</span><p>Build accessibility into the document or presentation, then check the exported result.</p></div></div><div class="checklist-bar" data-checklist="accessibility.html"><span class="checklist-progress" role="status" aria-live="polite">0 of 6 done</span><span class="checklist-meter" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></span><button type="button" data-checklist-reset>Clear ticks</button><button type="button" data-print>Print</button></div><section class="reading-section checklist"><h2>Content and structure</h2><ul class="check-list"><li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Use clear headings, descriptive links and a logical reading order.</span></label></li><li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Give informative images alternative text that conveys their purpose. Decorative images should be ignored by assistive technology, for example with empty alt text in HTML.</span></label></li><li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Caption video and provide an appropriate text alternative for audio.</span></label></li></ul></section><section class="reading-section checklist"><h2>Appearance and interaction</h2><ul class="check-list"><li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Use readable contrast: WCAG’s minimum is generally 4.5:1 for normal text and 3:1 for qualifying large text.</span></label></li><li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Do not rely on colour alone. Use labels, symbols or patterns too.</span></label></li><li><label><input type="checkbox"><span>Check keyboard access and focus visibility for interactive content.</span></label></li></ul></section><aside class="next-step"><div><h2>Check the relevant standard</h2><p>These checks are a starting point, not a claim that the work passes a full accessibility audit.</p></div><a href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/quickref/" class="text-link">Open the W3C reference ↗</a></aside><nav class="section-next" aria-label="More in How-to guides"><div class="section-next-head"><h2>More in How-to guides</h2><a class="related-all" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Self-Service Guides')">Self-service guides →</a></div><div class="related-grid"><a class="related-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Adobe Firefly')"><span class="related-next">Next</span><strong>Using AI image tools</strong><span>Use the current SKAO AI policy and approved tools before starting a task.</span></a><a class="related-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Making Your Own Poster')"><strong>Prepare a poster</strong><span>Confirm the organiser’s dimensions and output requirements before choosing a layout.</span></a><a class="related-card" href="$link.page('CRH', 'Preparing Files for Print')"><strong>Prepare files for print</strong><span>Use the supplier’s specifications for the actual product. A single export recipe does not fit every print job.</span></a></div></nav>
